        "content": "<p>I am aware that Lean4 allows you to do multi-inheritance using structures.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Haskell\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nf\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Int</span>\n<span class=\"nf\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Float</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">«</span><span class=\"kt\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Bar</span><span class=\"err\">»</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">extends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Foo</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kr\">where</span>\n\n<span class=\"nf\">axiom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">«</span><span class=\"kt\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Bar</span><span class=\"err\">»</span>\n<span class=\"o\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">fb</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- ℤ</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>But I don't want to create this third structure boilerplate when I may only need to use it for one-off terms. And it scales poorly when I add more types, like where I may have an intersection between 1 to 4 types (all of the combinations , so 2^n−1 ).</p>\n<p>I know there is no way to do this currently in Lean4. I want to ask if it is technically possible from the user side, perhaps through a macro or the notation system, to create my own infix type operator \"<code>∩</code>\" or similar to make the following </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">fb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span>\n<span class=\"n\">fb'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span>\n<span class=\"n\">fbq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Bar</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Qux</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>create terms whose types are like a structure that extends all of the types mentioned? The important bit is that I can type <code>fbq.</code> and see the fields of all three types.</p>",
